          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फिरणो — phirṇo — \"to wander about; to roam\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हूं काल बाजार मांय फिरसूं। hū̃ kāl bājār mā̃y phirsū̃. Tomorrow I'll wander round the market."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): वो बाजार मांय फिर्यो, vo bājār mā̃y phiryo."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फिरणो (phirṇo) is inherited from a reconstructed phirati, \"moves, wanders, turns\"; CDIAL lists the Old Marwari verb phiraï, \"turns, walks about\" (CDIAL 9078). फेर, again, is from the same family."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
